@startuml gas-deploy
' purpose: GasRack drag lifecycle — cost display,
'   ghost targeting, fail-safe miss path, cancel
'   contract, and compact density.
' covers: apps/starchess/src/presentation/hud/components/GasRack.tsx
' covers: apps/starchess/src/presentation/hud/components/GasRack.module.css
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/screens.puml
' related: _spec/apps/starchess/architecture/base-screen.puml
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

title StarChess · Gas deploy drag lifecycle

actor Player
participant "GasRack.tsx" as RACK <<app>>
database "MatchStore +\nmatchEconomy" as STORE <<db>>
participant "Live lesson board" as BOARD <<app>>

== Lift ==
Player ARROW_MAIN RACK : press canister
RACK ARROW_MAIN STORE : read gas + placement
RACK ARROW_MAIN RACK : anchor hint per lift\n(window listeners on)

== Hover ==
Player ARROW_MAIN RACK : travel over squares
RACK ARROW_MAIN BOARD : elementFromPoint\n[data-square]
RACK ARROW_MAIN STORE : resolve unit · cost · copy
RACK ARROW_OPTIONAL Player : preview + lifted buddies

== Drop ==
Player ARROW_MAIN RACK : release / Esc / blur
RACK ARROW_MAIN STORE : commitOrCancel\n(fail-safe to miss)
STORE ARROW_MAIN RACK : deploy target | null
RACK ARROW_MAIN BOARD : onDeploy(target)
RACK ARROW_ERROR RACK : fly home 240 ms,\nthen onCancel

' N_COST:
note over RACK
  Dropping a canister never spends gas; the
  armed special commits the cost when its action
  queues. Each unit declares its own price,
  defaulting to one, so heavy weapons lift
  additional canisters.
end note

' N_SAFE:
note over RACK
  Pointer capture is dispensable polish; window
  listeners carry every lift, because lost capture
  once stranded ghosts mid-screen. Unexpected
  board states degrade to the miss path, which
  flies the canister home.
end note

' N_TARGET:
note over RACK
  Deploys land on the unit that will occupy
  the square, queuing gas on its origin rather
  than its ghost. Vacated origins and unreadable
  mid-commit boards read as empty, sending the
  canister home.
end note

' N_HINT:
note over RACK
  The cancel hint anchors per lift, because the
  rack migrates between the footer region and
  the floating dock mid-session. Desktop clients
  name the escape key; touch clients keep only
  the drop-clear alternative.
end note

note over RACK
  Two reserve slots plus the ready canister
  fix capacity at three, with stable nodes so
  slides animate. Lifting advances the visible
  queue while drag counts reproduce the hovered
  unit price.
end note

@enduml
